Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.460
One surprising aspect of "Wednesday" has some&nbsp;
fans flocking to social media to fawn over star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.100
Jenna Ortega. It isn't her deadpan demeanor or the&nbsp;
character's sadistic impulses. It's pure talent.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.900
Since cartoonist Charles Addams introduced his&nbsp;
"Addams Family" cartoons in the late 1930s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.680
the beloved oddball family has been adapted&nbsp;
into live action on several occasions.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.600
First came the 1964 television series,&nbsp;
which ran for 64 episodes over two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.260
seasons. Despite its short run, the series&nbsp;
did an excellent job of bringing the Addams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:33.120
clan into mainstream pop culture, and the&nbsp;
original cast returned for a 1977 TV movie.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.680
Director Barry Sonnenfeld built upon this&nbsp;
groundwork in 1991 with his feature film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.200
"The Addams Family," which was followed by a 1993,&nbsp;
sequel, "Addams Family Values." For many fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.460
the undeniable standout of both features was&nbsp;
Christina Ricci's take on Wednesday Addams.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.180
Gomez and Morticia's stoic, twisted&nbsp;
daughter became a hit with moviegoers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.640
making Wednesday one of the most&nbsp;
popular members of the family.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.460
"I'm not perky."

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.660
It's a natural progression, then, to Netflix's&nbsp;
"Wednesday," a show all about the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.920
coming of age and solving a deadly mystery that&nbsp;
has plagued her family for years. "Wednesday"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.260
premiered on Netflix on November 23, 2022,&nbsp;
introducing subscribers to Jenna Ortega's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.680
version of the beloved character. For&nbsp;
the most part, audiences seem impressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.820
with what she has to offer as Wednesday, with&nbsp;
one aspect in particular really wowing them.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.660
Not long after "Wednesday" arrived on&nbsp;
Netflix, fans flocked to social media&nbsp;&nbsp;

